    "result_text": "Done. The build is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe rule: reject `POST /api/owners` with **429 Too Many Requests** once 100 or more owners already have a `registrationDate` of today.\n\nFollowing the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in this repo (modeled on the existing per-city capacity rule), I added four pieces:\n\n1. **`EnsureBelowDailyLimit`** (function) \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()`; throws `DailyOwnerLimitException` when the count is \u2265 100.\n2. **`DailyOwnerLimitException`** (checked exception) \u2014 so it appears in the `throws` clause and can be routed by an escalation handler.\n3. **`DailyOwnerLimitExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `429` with an `{errors: {dailyLimit: ...}}` body, matching the shape of the sibling capacity handler.\n4. **Wiring** \u2014 the escalation YAML `\u2026DailyOwnerLimitException.yml`, and a new `ensureBelowDailyLimit` step inserted into `owners.POST.yml` between `ensureCityBelowCapacity` and `build` (under the same `transaction` governance), so the check runs before the owner is constructed/saved.\n\nNew owners created via the endpoint default their `registrationDate` to today in `BuildOwner`, so each accepted create counts toward the limit \u2014 the 101st create today is rejected.",
